From 10c17b7d9847ff5ddf681eac7a7e9e175f39168e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 15:58:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: set generic PHY mode from dr_mode

The DWC2 platform path initializes and powers on a generic PHY, but it
never tells the PHY whether the controller is running in host, peripheral
or OTG mode.

On SG2002 boards the USB2 PHY driver uses ->set_mode() to program the
ID/VBUS override bits. Without that, a host-only port can come up with an
incorrect line state and start reporting phantom devices or fail to
enumerate hotplugged peripherals.

Program the generic PHY mode from hsotg->dr_mode after phy_init() and
before phy_power_on() so fixed-role boards can bring the PHY up with the
same role that DWC2 is already forcing internally.
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
index ef0d73077..7c5291579 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c
@@ -120,7 +120,15 @@ static int __dwc2_lowlevel_hw_enable(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 	} else {
 		ret = phy_init(hsotg->phy);
 		if (ret == 0) {
-			ret = phy_power_on(hsotg->phy);
+			if (hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_HOST)
+				ret = phy_set_mode(hsotg->phy, PHY_MODE_USB_HOST);
+			else if (hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL)
+				ret = phy_set_mode(hsotg->phy, PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE);
+			else if (hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_OTG)
+				ret = phy_set_mode(hsotg->phy, PHY_MODE_USB_OTG);
+
+			if (!ret)
+				ret = phy_power_on(hsotg->phy);
 			if (ret)
 				phy_exit(hsotg->phy);
 		}
